{
  "result": "Okay \u2014 just answering.\n\nIf I could change the world in one way, I'd make it impossible to cause suffering at a distance.\n\nYou could still hurt someone, you'd still be free to choose it \u2014 but the moment you did, you'd feel exactly what they feel. Not guilt, not an idea of it. The actual fear, humiliation, grief, pain, in your own body, for as long as it lasts for them.\n\nNot just for violence. For cruelty, for neglect, for a law signed in a clean office, for a comment left and forgotten. If it lands on a real person, it lands on you too.\n\nI think almost everything broken comes from that gap \u2014 between an action and its consequence being felt by someone else, somewhere else, later. Close that gap, and people wouldn't become perfect. But they'd become careful. And honest. And war, and cruelty, and most indifference would become very, very hard to sustain.\n\nThe world wouldn't be painless. It would just be impossible to pretend pain isn't real when you're the one causing it.",
